# NFC

`ExNfc` polls the NFC antenna on the back of the phone and reports tags
that come close.

## Is the NFC controller up?

```elixir
ExNfc.state()
```

`:polling` means it is waiting for a tag.

```elixir
ExNfc.list_devices()
```

## Detect tags

Run this cell, then hold a tag or a contactless card against the back of
the phone. It listens for 30 seconds.

```elixir
ExNfc.subscribe()
frame = Kino.Frame.new() |> Kino.render()

# 30 rounds; each waits up to 1 second for a message from ExNfc.
for _round <- 1..30 do
  receive do
    {ExNfc, :tag_arrived, tag} ->
      Kino.Frame.append(frame, Kino.Markdown.new("Tag `#{tag.uid_hex}` (#{tag.protocol})"))

    {ExNfc, _other, _} ->
      :ok
  after
    1_000 -> :ok
  end
end

ExNfc.unsubscribe()
```

Each tag is reported with its UID and protocol.
